%% DM26-0670

%% A client publishes on a topic. The path is the code as built (2026-10-21, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md);
%% the decision at the Listener is the design (docs/architecture/policy-enforcement.md, stage 5), not built yet. The
%% agent's own check before it sends is built (stage 1, 2026-10-21: the same rule as the broker's, topic_gate.rs).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Own as the agent's check and its PolicyActor<br/>(built, stage 1)
    participant Client as Agent (TcpClientActor)
    participant Listener
    participant Policy as Broker's PolicyLookup<br/>(designed)
    participant Session as SessionAgent
    participant Broker
    participant Topic as TopicManager / TopicAgent
    participant Sub as SubscriberAgent
    participant Peer as each subscriber's session

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Own,Client: BUILT 2026-10-21 (stage 1), not yet run on a cluster: before anything is sent
    Client->>Own: publish, topic
    alt the agent's policy speaks
        Own-->>Client: permit (even outside the computed set) or forbid (even inside it)
    else no policy yet, or it does not speak
        Own-->>Client: the computed set: declared and implied topics
    end
    alt refused
        Client->>Client: log it, ClientEvent::PublishRefused, nothing sent
    end
    end

    Client->>Listener: PublishRequest(registration_id, topic, payload, share_identity)
    alt no active session, or another session's id
        Listener-->>Client: ErrorMessage("Bad request: ...")
    end
    Listener->>Listener: published_by = the connection's identity, when share_identity

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Listener,Policy: DESIGNED: the decision
    Listener->>Policy: publish, Topic::"topic", Identity::"identity",<br/>facts: workload, declared or implied
    alt policy loaded and it speaks
        Policy-->>Listener: Allow or Deny
    else no policy, or it does not speak
        Listener->>Listener: the floor: implied topics from the identity,<br/>declared topics from the certificate's p:pub: names
    end
    alt refused (default deny)
        Listener-->>Client: PublishResponse(Err "refused: ...")
        Note right of Client: ClientEvent::PublishRefused (stage 0), no PublishAcknowledged
    end
    end

    Listener->>Session: PublishRequest(topic, payload, published_by)
    Session->>Broker: PublishRequest(reply_to: the session)
    Broker->>Topic: handle_publish_request (a topic is created on first use)
    alt the topic has subscribers
        Topic->>Sub: PublishResponse(topic, payload, published_by)
        Sub->>Peer: push the message
        Peer-->>Peer: the subscriber reads published_by and may check it
    else no subscribers yet
        Topic->>Topic: queue it for the first subscriber
    end
    Topic-->>Session: PublishRequestAck
    Session-->>Client: PublishRequestAck (ClientEvent::PublishAcknowledged)
